  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number of hours of a laptop's battery life. Then we have $X\u223cN(8,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find $P(X<6).$ But first, we need to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X>11)=0.20.$ First, we convert this to a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 11) & =1-P(X>11) \\\\  & =1-0.20 \\\\  & =0.80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 11) & =0.80 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{11-8}{\\sigma }) & =0.80 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.80 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.80)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.80)=0.8416.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =0.8416 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{0.8416} \\\\ \\sigma  & \u22483.5646.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve for $P(X\\le 6)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =P(Z\\le \\frac{6-8}{3.5646}) \\\\  & \u2248P(Z\\le -0.56) \\\\  & =\u03a6(-0.56) \\\\  & =0.2877 \\\\  & \u224828.8%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $28.8%$ of laptops will last less than $6$ hours on a single charge.",
